      "id": "2105930323913798107",
      "text": "RT @mstockton: For folks not understanding where we are at with AI now - if the task is verifiable, it is now solved by AI.\n\nYes, earlier d…",
      "created_at": "Fri Oct 02 07:58:10 +0000 2026",
      "lang": "en",
      "media": [],
      "retweet": {
        "id": "2105857523668451416",
        "text": "For folks not understanding where we are at with AI now - if the task is verifiable, it is now solved by AI.\n\nYes, earlier days you could argue that 'AI isn't that good' (e.g. see first attached chart here, where GPT-4o underperformed average accountants on tasks)\n\nBut now, it's a totally different story (only ~2 years later). The second chart is astounding. It took me a while to even understand it because it looks so odd. It compares manual accounting tasks to tasks complete with Opus 5.5. Basically Opus 5.5. solves all tasks almost instantly at a 100% accuracy rate, whereas a person takes a lot more time and gets a lot of things wrong. It makes the chart look entirely silly because the axes aren't even comparable.\n\nSo yeah, this is where we're at. If it is verifiable, it is solved. This is just how these model architectures work now.",
        "created_at": "Fri Oct 02 03:08:53 +0000 2026",
        "lang": "en",
        "media": [],
        "retweet": null,
        "quoted": {
          "id": "2105766686213410845",
          "text": "On these detail-oriented, well-specified tasks, frontier models are now faster and more accurate than accountants, even the best one in our study. https://t.co/j40WelCfiN",
          "created_at": "Thu Oct 01 21:07:55 +0000 2026",
          "lang": "en",
